## Canonical chunk fixture shape

Keep chunking-related fixture data canonical and model-driven.

### Use the existing chunk model shape

- Represent topics, code blocks, tables, images, info blocks, and text chunks with the existing chunk model fields.
- Keep chunk content in `RawContent` / `Data` / `RelatedChunksIndexes` instead of adding parallel raw variants.
- Do not add helper properties that duplicate the same chunk meaning in another form.

### Keep fixture fields minimal

- Add only the fields needed for the scenario under test.
- Prefer explicit fixture builders for code block counts, topic depth, and mixed-content layouts instead of baking those into a model.
- If a scenario needs a strange or malformed text sample, keep that as input text rather than a new model type.

